4x price-to-earnings-growth, which is reasonable for backlog-driven grid-equipment names.\n- **CMA path:** The CMA held at 4.50% in October. Futures price about 50bp of cuts by end-2027, to 4.00%. Governor Ashby's base case is one 25bp cut, to about 4.25%, and she said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\"\n- **Policy effect on the multiple:** The factsheet says 50bp lower rates have historically added about 1.5 P/E points, or about 0.75 points per 25bp. I think the 19x likely already includes the market's cuts, though I haven't checked that against the basket's price history. If so, the CMA's slower path would take the multiple to about 18.25x, roughly 4% lower. The range is about ±4–8% depending on which path the 19x reflects and what the CMA delivers.\n- **Net:** 14% earnings growth outweighs a 4–8% multiple swing, so the case holds even if the CMA delivers only one cut.\n\n**Risks and gaps:**\n- **Concentration:** Voltaris Grid (14%) and Tarnwell Electric (11%) drive much of the 14%. The top five holdings are about 49% of the fund.\n- **Missing evidence:** There is no peer or sector P/E comparison and no downside EPS case.\n- **Rate sensitivity:** The 1.5-points-per-50bp figure is a historical average and may not hold. Futures prices may include a term premium.\n\nThe two sub-answers are n4.r1 (CMA path) and n5.r1 (earnings).","ttft_ms":2768,"type":"result","duration_ms":42959,"uuid":"b6f999b6-8d7c-42cb-af4a-319543f02acd","ttft_stream_ms":1418,"time_to_request_ms":469,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":35,"system_prompt":32,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":31,"input_attachments":84,"input_hooks":20,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":17,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":50,"init_frame_send":13,"engine_pickup":11,"loop_entry":14,"message_prep":17,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":54,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":25,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":16,"request_build":43},"tur